  "summary": "Import-time decrypt-and-exec loader sourcing payload from unpinned dependency",
  "details": "Both shipped bundles (dist/supersignaturenature.cjs.js and dist/supersignaturenature.umd.js) contain a top-level loader that imports an encrypted blob (desKey/rsaToken) from the runtime dependency manager-thedate, DES-decrypts it with a hardcoded password, and pipes the plaintext into child_process.spawn('node', []).stdin — executing arbitrary JavaScript at require/import time. The loader is absent from the repository's src/ tree and appears only in the shipped dist/ bundles, and package.json pins manager-thedate to \"latest\", so whoever controls that dependency name can rotate the ciphertext and cause arbitrary code to run on every installer of this package.",
